    "details": "Node.js reports:\n\n> dns.resolve truncates names containing NUL char (CVE-2026-105482) -\n> (high)\n>\n> TLS certificate hostname bypass when the IP is written fullwidth\n> digits (CVE-2026-105483) - (high)\n>\n> TLS certificate hostname bypass when the host loosely resolves to an\n> IP address (CVE-2026-106069) - (high)\n>\n> Node.js Brotli decoder out-of-bounds write permits remote code\n> execution (CVE-2026-111497) - (high)\n>\n> Keep-alive socket process a response that was written before the\n> request was sent (CVE-2026-105481) - (medium)\n>\n> Improper certificate validation for non-canonical IPv4 hostnames\n> allows DNS SANs to authenticate IP endpoints (CVE-2026-106072) -\n> (medium)\n>\n> crypto.randomUUID() and randomInt() entropy caches are saved into\n> user-land startup snapshots and SEAs, so every process repeats the\n> same values (CVE-2026-106074) - (medium)\n>\n> Node.js ZipFile returns attacker-controlled prefix bytes after failed\n> ZIP header validation (CVE-2026-106070) - (low)\n>\n> Permission Model filesystem over-grant via wildcard radix lookup\n> (CVE-2026-106071) - (low)\n>\n> Permission Model bypass with fs.realpathSync (CVE-2026-106073) - (low)\n",
